// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A nested function is minted: a `fn` declared inside a body is a closure
// record built where it is declared (its captures, or an empty record when
// it captures nothing), so the declaring frame performs `Alloc`, and a
// function declaring `!Alloc` around it is refused.
// Every maker that returns its nested stage (`fn lowpass_filter(sr) = { fn
// stage(x) = …; stage }`) built one with a row of `Pure` until the
// allocation audit's first frontier run.
fn adder(k) with !Alloc = {
  fn add(x) = x + k
  add
}

fn main() = adder(40)(2)
